    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nRetry the four image-build steps once when they exit with code 1, matching the rule the AMD and CPU image builds in `.buildkite/hardware_tests/` already use.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `image-build`, `arm64-image-build`, `image-build-cpu` and `cpu-arm64-image-build` retry once on exit code 1, as well as on the existing agent-lost exit codes (`-1`, `-10`).\n- A transient failure while fetching from an upstream source no longer fails the whole build and skips every downstream test step. Examples: a package index, a GitHub release download, or an apt mirror mid-sync.\n\n## Validation\n\n- The YAML parses, and each of the four steps lists the rules `-1`, `-10` and `1`.\n- Retry rules only take effect in a real build, so the effect will be measured from CI history after merge: how many retries fire on exit 1, how many pass on retry, and how many fail twice.\n\n## Details\n\nImage-build steps run no tests, so one retry on exit 1 can't hide a test failure. A real build breakage fails again on the retry and the build fails as before, at the cost of one extra image build. A step-level rule covers every fetch site in the Dockerfile and the build scripts, including ones added later, without a retry loop at each site. The rule and its comment are copied from `.buildkite/hardware_tests/amd.yaml`.\n\nThese steps also build the `TORCH_NIGHTLY=1` images, so those get the retry too. The non-root smoke-test step runs the built image, so it is left unchanged, and so is the HPU image step.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
